description:
Create an isolated interview environment in VSCode at '/home/ga/interview_workspace/'. Requirements: 1) Create workspace directory '/home/ga/interview_workspace/' and subdirectory '.vscode/'. 2) Create '.vscode/settings.json' with the following settings: 'workbench.colorTheme' set to 'Default Light+', 'editor.fontSize' set to 14, 'files.autoSave' set to 'afterDelay', 'editor.minimap.enabled' set to false, 'workbench.activityBar.visible' set to false. 3) Create '.vscode/tasks.json' with a 'tasks' array containing three task objects: first task with 'label' as 'Run Python', 'type' as 'shell', 'command' as 'python3 ${file}', second task with 'label' as 'Run JavaScript', 'type' as 'shell', 'command' as 'node ${file}', third task with 'label' as 'Run Java', 'type' as 'shell', 'command' as 'bash -c "javac ${file} && java ${fileBasenameNoExtension}"'. Also set 'version' to '2.0.0' in tasks.json. 4) Create three starter files in workspace root: 'starter.py' containing '# Technical Interview

def solve_problem():
    pass

if __name__ == "__main__":
    solve_problem()', 'starter.js' containing '// Technical Interview

function solveProblem() {
    // TODO
}

solveProblem();', 'Starter.java' containing '// Technical Interview

public class Starter {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        solveProblem();
    }

    public static void solveProblem() {
        // TODO
    }
}'. 5) Open VSCode with the interview_workspace directory.
